  "fps": 30,
  "text": "Every single night millions of men sit in a parked car for 10 quiet minutes. They're not listening to music. They're not on calls. So what are they doing? Between the boss screaming at 11am, rent notices at 3pm and family expectations at 8pm, a man becomes an emotional filter. He can't tell his parents, they'll panic. He can't tell his partner, she's already stressed. His only reply. Subsorted hair, bro. Globally, men are 3.5 times less likely to ask for help, carrying silent pressure until it breaks them. So why does he park in the driveway and just freeze? You see, that quiet car is the only place on earth where he doesn't have to be a protector, a provider or strong. For 10 minutes, he's just human. This mains day, don't ask him to fix something. Just ask him, bhai, to thik hai na.",
