  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.8,
      "text": "Every single night millions of men sit in a parked car for 10 quiet minutes."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.44,
      "end": 11.4,
      "text": "They're not listening to music. They're not on calls. So what are they doing?"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.28,
      "end": 20.14,
      "text": "Between the boss screaming at 11am, rent notices at 3pm and family expectations at 8pm,"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.44,
      "end": 25.6,
      "text": "a man becomes an emotional filter. He can't tell his parents, they'll panic."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.42,
      "end": 31.5,
      "text": "He can't tell his partner, she's already stressed. His only reply."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.48,
      "end": 39.3,
      "text": "Subsorted hair, bro. Globally, men are 3.5 times less likely to ask for help,"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.64,
      "end": 45.62,
      "text": "carrying silent pressure until it breaks them. So why does he park in the driveway and just"
    },
    {
      "start": 45.62,
      "end": 51.9,
      "text": "freeze? You see, that quiet car is the only place on earth where he doesn't have to be"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.9,
      "end": 57.38,
      "text": "a protector, a provider or strong. For 10 minutes, he's just human."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.22,
      "end": 64.68,
      "text": "This mains day, don't ask him to fix something. Just ask him, bhai, to thik hai na."
    }
  ]
}
